From 1f65aa501993862302549f1ea62f852c2bd6b75d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:32:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: book a continued run's clean exit as a
 protocol violation; no live-run promise once its worker exited

Incident (hermes-worker-6, 2026-11-13, t_01a1d563324d7e8e run 11569): the gateway restarted at 15:39Z and
the run's turn was checkpointed and continued by the next owner. The continued worker hit the tool-loop
stop and exited rc=0 at 15:55Z without kanban_complete/block/schedule. No events followed; the card stayed
`running` with both pids dead until a manual reclaim at 16:06Z, and `hermes kanban comment` at 16:05Z said
"The card has a live worker run: it gets this note at its next model call".

Five whys (replica events of run 41156 / local 11569, code at origin/main b3745e62d5):
1. Why did it stay running? `_reclaim_dead_workers` (hermes_cli/kanban_db_dispatch.py:1336-1338)
   got `hold=True` from `reclaim_proof` and skipped the row every tick.
2. Why hold? `reclaim_proof` (kanban_failed_result.py:184-189) holds whenever no proof is found and
   `modern_result_recorded` is true. The stopping owner's restart booking (`worker_result` exit 76,
   `death_proof_version: 1`, `result_role: owner_restart`, `result_sequence: 2`) made the run modern.
3. Why no proof? `attributable_events` (kanban_failed_result_identity.py:154-190) could not pick a
   result: the owner booking's causal snapshot no longer covers the later binding, and the continued
   worker's rc=0 `worker_result` carried no `result_sequence`/`bound_event_identity`, so the sequence
   check failed and `_observed_history` found nothing. `failed_result_receipt` also rejects `code == 0`.
4. Why was the rc=0 result unmarked? `_record_worker_result` (gateway/session_kanban.py:414) only wrote
   death-proof identity for a nonzero code (`if code and ...`): the modern contract was built for failed
   results, and a clean exit was left to the legacy `managed_run_exit_code` path, which a modern run
   never reaches because of the hold.
5. Why did nothing else notice? Every other reclaim path defers to the same modern veto
   (`owner_reclaim_blocked` -> `modern_result_recorded`), and the comment paths read only the task's
   `running` status (`kanban_db.live_run_id`).
The hypotheses in the card: the stale `worker_pid`/claim_lock were not the cause (the sweep did pair the
dead outer pid 1110350 with the run); the owner does book `worker_result`, but in a shape the modern
selector cannot attribute.

Fix:
- `_record_worker_result`: a clean exit also writes the death-proof identity fields when the run already
  holds modern evidence (a continued turn). Plain runs are unchanged (still unmarked rc=0, legacy path).
  The failed-result observer is still armed only for nonzero codes.
- `failed_result_receipt(allow_clean=...)`: the dispatcher sweep (`reclaim_proof`, not the observer)
  accepts a modern exit 0. Every recorded process of the run must still be gone (`failed_result_proof`).
  The sweep then classifies rc=0 as `protocol_violation` with the worker's last output, as for a plain run.
- New `hermes_cli/kanban_comment_liveness.py`: `kanban_comment` (tool) and `hermes kanban comment` (CLI)
  stop promising a live run when the run's final worker_result is booked after its last binding and
  admission (a continuable checkpoint is not final), or every pid this host recorded for it is dead.
  They say the note waits for the card's next run; the tool returns `live_run: false, worker_exited: true`.

Tests:
- RED on origin/main, GREEN here: test_a_continued_run_whose_worker_exits_cleanly_is_a_protocol_violation
  (status stays running on main; here one detect_crashed_workers pass -> ready, run crashed with
  protocol_violation metadata, error and last_failure_error start with _PROTOCOL_VIOLATION_ERROR and
  quote the worker's last output, one protocol_violation event).
- Guards: a continued run whose worker fails is still a crash; a live continued interpreter with a clean
  result still holds the run.
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_comment_liveness.py: CLI and tool on an exited continued run; a live worker
  and a checkpointed turn with a live submitter keep the live-run promise.
- Unchanged plain path: test_kanban_managed_worker_loss.py, test_kanban_failed_result_reconcile.py,
  test_kanban_worker_owner_restart.py, test_kanban_board_delivery.py pass.
